Z||000000||TheHans||12-12-2000||01:30 AM||||Hey there Fiero Friends<P>I have an 85 2.5l.<BR>It will not idle in Drive.<BR>It tries to, but It just dies out.<BR>It also has a horrible hesitation and will not take off. <BR>My gas milage is really (really) bad.<BR>The integrator is at 80.<BR>I can smell gas out of the exhaust.<BR>There is no vacuum leak (that I can find)<BR>The IACV is working.<BR>The the egr seems OK.<BR>I am thinking it may be a leaky injector or the fuel regulator.<BR>Does anyone know what the fuel pressure should be?  <BR>How can I check for the injector, or a sure fire way to check if the regulator is working right?<BR>If anyone has some good ideas please help.<BR>Ive spend a lot of time and money on her and<BR>don't want to do the shotgun method. (blast her with all new parts and hope for the best)<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||12-12-2000||11:56 AM||||I had a leaky 2.5 injector.. Take off the air filter, and then have someone crank the car while you watch. It should pulse in a cone shape. Mine kept dripping and dripping even after the car was off. Until all the pressure was gone. Are youg etting a code?||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheHans||12-12-2000||07:31 PM||||Thanks for the tip.<BR>Does anyone know how to check if the fuel regulator is stuck open/closed/working?<BR>I haven't checked the codes yet.<BR>I just drove it 300 miles home after the rebuild. It would start missing at about 60-65 mph. Would this be the EGR? <BR>Would that also have an effect on the idle problem and the rich mixture that I seem to be having?<BR>I watched the injector with a time light it looked ok. Is there some more basic tests I can perform on the injector?||||reg||1
